<!-- ============================================================
     PROTOTYPE: Reading comprehension — proof that graph doesn't
     cross the x-axis (completing the square)
     Bickerton & Sangwin approach: present numbered proof, ask
     questions about structure, justification, and meaning.
     ============================================================ -->
<question type="stack">
  <name><text>PROTOTYPE: Reading comprehension — graph and x-axis</text></name>
  <questiontext format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[
<p>Here is a proof that the graph of \(y = {@quad_expr@}\) does not cross the \(x\)-axis.</p>

<div class="proof" style="border-left:3px solid #003399; padding:8px 16px; margin:12px 0; background:#f8f8ff;">
<p><strong>Proof</strong></p>
<p><strong>(1)</strong> \({@quad_expr@} = {@expand_step@}\)</p>
<p><strong>(2)</strong> \(= {@csq_expr@}\)</p>
<p><strong>(3)</strong> \({@csq_inner@} \geq 0\) for all values of \(x\).</p>
<p><strong>(4)</strong> Therefore \({@quad_expr@} \geq {@qval@}\) for all values of \(x\).</p>
<p><strong>(5)</strong> Since \({@qval@} > 0\), the expression \({@quad_expr@}\) is always positive, so the graph of \(y = {@quad_expr@}\) never reaches the \(x\)-axis.</p>
</div>

<p>Answer the following questions about the proof above.</p>

<ol class="HELM_parts">
  <li><p>In which step is completing the square carried out?</p>
      <p>Steps [[input:ans1]] and [[input:ans2]] [[validation:ans1]] [[validation:ans2]] [[feedback:prt1]]</p></li>

  <li><p>What property of a square number is used in step (3)?</p>
      <p>[[input:ans3]] [[validation:ans3]] [[feedback:prt2]]</p></li>

  <li><p>What is the minimum value of \({@quad_expr@}\)?</p>
      <p>[[input:ans4]] [[validation:ans4]] [[feedback:prt3]]</p></li>

  <li><p>At what value of \(x\) does this minimum occur?</p>
      <p>\(x = \) [[input:ans5]] [[validation:ans5]] [[feedback:prt4]]</p></li>

  <li><p>Would the proof still work if the constant term were \({@c_counter@}\) instead of \({@c@}\)?</p>
      <p>[[input:ans6]] [[validation:ans6]] [[feedback:prt5]]</p></li>
</ol>
    ]]></text>
  </questiontext>
  <generalfeedback format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[
<ol class="HELM_parts">
  <li><p>Steps <strong>(1)</strong> and <strong>(2)</strong> carry out the completing the square: step (1) rewrites \({@x^2 + b*x@}\) using the identity \({@x^2 + b*x@} = {@csq_inner@} - {@bsq@}\), and step (2) combines the constants.</p></li>
  <li><p>The property used is that <strong>a square is always greater than or equal to zero</strong>: \({@csq_inner@} \geq 0\).</p></li>
  <li><p>The minimum value is \({@qval@}\), achieved when \({@csq_inner@} = 0\).</p></li>
  <li><p>This occurs when \(x = {@-half_b@}\).</p></li>
  <li><p>No. With constant term \({@c_counter@}\) the completed-square form would be \({@csq_inner@} + {@qval_counter@}\). Since \({@qval_counter@} \leq 0\), the expression can equal zero or be negative, so the graph would cross or touch the \(x\)-axis and the proof would fail.</p></li>
</ol>
    ]]></text>
  </generalfeedback>
